# NexusOS Tor Configuration
# ========================
# Transparent proxy: routes all traffic through Tor
# Based on Tor Project's transparent proxy guide

# Tor configuration file — copy to /etc/tor/torrc

## Basic Configuration
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
PidFile /var/run/tor/tor.pid
Log notice file /var/log/tor/notices.log
Log warn file /var/log/tor/warnings.log

## Transparent Proxy — route all traffic through Tor
TransPort 9040
TransListenAddress 127.0.0.1
DNSPort 5353
DNSListenAddress 127.0.0.1

## SOCKS Proxy for applications that support it
SocksPort 9050
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050 IsolateDestAddr
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.1/32
SocksPolicy reject *

## Exit policy — allow common ports, block the rest
ExitPolicy accept *:80,443     # HTTP/HTTPS
ExitPolicy accept *:53          # DNS
ExitPolicy accept *:22          # SSH
ExitPolicy accept *:993,995     # Encrypted mail
ExitPolicy accept *:6660-6669   # IRC
ExitPolicy accept *:6697        # IRC over TLS
ExitPolicy reject *

## Circuit settings — shorter lifetime for more anonymity
MaxCircuitDirtiness 600
CircuitBuildTimeout 30
CircuitStreamTimeout 60
NewCircuitPeriod 30
NumEntryGuards 8

## Performance
AvoidDiskWrites 1
ClientUseIPv4 1
ClientUseIPv6 1

## Security
SafeLogging 1
ClientPreferSOCKSNoAuth 0
ClientDNSRejectInternalAddresses 1
ClientRejectInternalAddresses 1
DownloadExtraInfo 1

## Hidden Services (if hosting)
#HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/nexusos/
#HiddenServicePort 80 127.0.0.1:80
#HiddenServicePort 443 127.0.0.1:443

## Bridges (for censorship circumvention)
# UseBridges 1
# UpdateBridgesFromAuthority 1
# Bridge obfs4 IP:PORT FINGERPRINT CERT=... iat-mode=0